# The editor's keys (K3; scenes/parts.seed.ts writes the note into a scratch outline): a block opened to be written,
# and what an editor's keys make of it, each by the act its key runs. Return begins a list's next item, a step is
# ticked, a line is moved over the one above, and a word is selected and wrapped: with something selected the hint
# row under the field offers what is done with it, beside the keys that are always there.
bar.open scope=search query="Frost fleece"
bar.pick n=1
edit
draft.newline
draft.paste text="- fleece from the shed"
draft.newline
draft.paste text="pegs"
draft.check
draft.check
draft.newline
draft.paste text="bricks for the corners"
draft.line op=up
draft.select what=word
draft.wrap with=**
